<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaston, Duke of Orléans</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1608">1608</a>–<a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Gaston of Orléans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaston, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, was the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiii-of-france">Louis XIII of France</a> and for many years heir to the throne. He took part in repeated plots against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a>, and in 1632 secretly married Marguerite of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, sister of Duke Charles IV, which helped provoke the French invasion of Lorraine. He later sided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-fronde">Fronde</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-mazarin">Cardinal Mazarin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaston-duke-of-orleans.jpg" alt="Gaston, Duke of Orléans" width="320" height="524" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthony van Dyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Full_length_portrait_painting_of_Gaston_of_France,_Duke_of_Orl%C3%A9ans_in_1634_by_Anthony_van_Dyck_(Mus%C3%A9e_Cond%C3%A9).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
